
"smart_sources:- WyoHistory.org - Before the Numbers_ Naming Wyoming’s Highways.md": {"path":"- WyoHistory.org - Before the Numbers_ Naming Wyoming’s Highways.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"bchpc4","at":1785794996639},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783617081170,"size":33759,"at":1785794996921,"hash":"bchpc4"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,6],"#":[7,148],"##Resources":[149,182],"##Resources#Sources":[151,175],"##Resources#Sources#{1}":[153,153],"##Resources#Sources#{2}":[154,154],"##Resources#Sources#{3}":[155,155],"##Resources#Sources#{4}":[156,156],"##Resources#Sources#{5}":[157,157],"##Resources#Sources#{6}":[158,158],"##Resources#Sources#{7}":[159,159],"##Resources#Sources#{8}":[160,160],"##Resources#Sources#{9}":[161,161],"##Resources#Sources#{10}":[162,162],"##Resources#Sources#{11}":[163,163],"##Resources#Sources#{12}":[164,164],"##Resources#Sources#{13}":[165,165],"##Resources#Sources#{14}":[166,166],"##Resources#Sources#{15}":[167,167],"##Resources#Sources#{16}":[168,168],"##Resources#Sources#{17}":[169,169],"##Resources#Sources#{18}":[170,170],"##Resources#Sources#{19}":[171,171],"##Resources#Sources#{20}":[172,172],"##Resources#Sources#{21}":[173,173],"##Resources#Sources#{22}":[174,175],"##Resources#Illustrations":[176,182],"##Resources#Illustrations#{1}":[178,178],"##Resources#Illustrations#{2}":[179,179],"##Resources#Illustrations#{3}":[180,180],"##Resources#Illustrations#{4}":[181,181],"##Resources#Illustrations#{5}":[182,182]},"outlinks":[{"title":"thorough history on this website","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/lincoln-highway-wyoming","line":11},{"title":"Good Roads Movement promoters Jake Schwoob and Gus Holm, in the front car here, were in the caravan of the first cars to enter Yellowstone, 1915. Growth in auto travel to national parks was one of the main drivers behind the naming of national highways in the 1910s and ‘20s, when most of them were still dirt. Park County Archives.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways1.jpg?itok=Ol8SoNV_","line":15,"embedded":true},{"title":"By 1918, an American Automobile Association map of transcontinental routes sported logos for two dozen named higways. Library of Congress. Click to enlarge","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways3.jpg?itok=2vxej_MJ","line":19,"embedded":true},{"title":"This 1916 postcard presents Cody, Wyo., as the center of the world, with Salt Lake and Seattle just over the hills. In the foreground, six named highways funnel cars (with pennants from New York, Massachusetts, Maine, Minnesota, Iowa, Georgia and California) into Cody. The Henry Ford museum.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/medium/public/highways2.jpg?itok=nw2KSNjG","line":31,"embedded":true},{"title":"Black and Yellow Trail","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/let-us-ramble-exploring-black-and-yellow-trail-wyoming","line":43},{"title":"1901 Burlington Rail route","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/burlington-route-wyomings-second-transcontinental-railroad","line":47},{"title":"Gus Holm, of Cody, Wyo. The Park County Enterprise called him  the 'chief good road booster of all Wyoming.' Park County Archives.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/small/public/highways4.jpg?itok=_faBse9O","line":49,"embedded":true},{"title":"Robert Reamer","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/wyoming-parkitecture","line":61},{"title":"Departing Aug. 26, 1920, a party of twelve motorists formally inaugurated the National Park-to-Park Highway with a 76-day tour starting with the Denver-to-Yellowstone trek through Wyoming. This map was published in 1922. Amercianroads.us.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways5.jpg?itok=AI0hx3PR","line":75,"embedded":true},{"title":"The 1920 Park-to-Park caravan paused in Casper, Wyo., on a new concrete bridge over the North Platte, with the Midwest Refinery and Casper Mountain in the background. Park County Archives.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways6.jpg?itok=4oUt3I4x","line":79,"embedded":true},{"title":"The Custer Battlefield Highway, designated in 1919, ran from Des Moines, Iowa, to Glacier National Park. The route traversed northeast Wyoming from Beulah to Parkman and passed through its namesake national cemetery in Montana. This map, published in 1925, aimed in part to press the federal government to pay for more roads. Library of Congress.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways7.jpg?itok=hWs0W8Z9","line":111,"embedded":true},{"title":"Good roads promoter Jake Schwoob of Cody owned one of Wyoming’s first car dealerships, and developed the county-based numbering system for Wyoming license plates. Here he is in 1923 by his Lincoln, bearing Wyoming license plate #1. American Heritage Center.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways8.jpg?itok=zgEcMyxQ","line":115,"embedded":true},{"title":"Tourist cars head toward Cody from Yellowstone Park on the road along the Buffalo Bill Reservoir. In the late 1920s the federal government began a system of numbered routes, as there were so many named highways the system was chaotic and confusing. While the new system lost romance, it gained efficiency. F.J. Hiscock photo, Park County Archives.","target":"https://www.wyohistory.org/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/highways9.jpg?itok=ucGqcDv4","line":145,"embedded":true},{"title":"http://www.encyclopediadubuque.org/index.php?title=ATLANTIC,\\_YELLOWSTONE,\\_PACIFIC\\_HIGHWAY","target":"http://www.encyclopediadubuque.org/index.php?title=ATLANTIC,_YELLOWSTONE,_PACIFIC_HIGHWAY \"(opens in a new window","line":153},{"title":"https://www.sweetwaternow.com/flaming-gorge-green-river-basin-scenic-byway-designated-as-all-american-road/","target":"https://www.sweetwaternow.com/flaming-gorge-green-river-basin-scenic-byway-designated-as-all-american-road/ \"(opens in a new window","line":154},{"title":"https://books.google.com/books?id=6bG8b\\_-ER2sC&pg=RA7-PA38&lpg=RA7-PA38&d","target":"https://books.google.com/books?id=6bG8b_-ER2sC&pg=RA7-PA38&lpg=RA7-PA38&d \"(opens in a new window","line":155},{"title":"https://books.google.com/books?id=BV5GAQAAMAAJ&pg=RA7-PA43&dq=%22george+washington+highway%22+omaha+savannah&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks\\_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj369ej\\_OnvAhXPrZ4KHbdyC5sQ6AEwAHoECAAQAg#v=onepage&q=%22george%20washington%20highway%22%20omaha%20savannah&f=false","target":"https://books.google.com/books?id=BV5GAQAAMAAJ&pg=RA7-PA43&dq=%22george+washington+highway%22+omaha+savannah&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj369ej_OnvAhXPrZ4KHbdyC5sQ6AEwAHoECAAQAg#v=onepage&q=%22george%20washington%20highway%22%20omaha%20savannah&f=false \"(opens in a new window","line":156},{"title":"https://books.google.com/books?id=\\_R1IAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA819","target":"https://books.google.com/books?id=_R1IAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA819 \"(opens in a new window","line":157},{"title":"https://sites.rootsweb.com/~wytttp/history/bartlett/chapter33.htm","target":"https://sites.rootsweb.com/~wytttp/history/bartlett/chapter33.htm \"(opens in a new window","line":159},{"title":"https://www.nps.gov/parkhistory/online\\_books/yell\\_roads/hrs1-5.htm","target":"https://www.nps.gov/parkhistory/online_books/yell_roads/hrs1-5.htm \"(opens in a new window","line":162},{"title":"https://iowadot.gov/autotrails/custerbattlefieldhighway","target":"https://iowadot.gov/autotrails/custerbattlefieldhighway \"(opens in a new window","line":164},{"title":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/publicroads/06jul/03.cfm","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/publicroads/06jul/03.cfm \"(opens in a new window","line":165},{"title":"https://archive.org/stream/officialrouteboo00yell/officialrouteboo00yell\\_djvu.txt","target":"https://archive.org/stream/officialrouteboo00yell/officialrouteboo00yell_djvu.txt \"(opens in a new window","line":166},{"title":"https://pavingtheway.tv/","target":"https://pavingtheway.tv/ \"(opens in a new window","line":169},{"title":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/publicroads/16novdec/03.cfm","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/publicroads/16novdec/03.cfm \"(opens in a new window","line":170},{"title":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/infrastructure/numbers.cfm","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/infrastructure/numbers.cfm \"(opens in a new window","line":171},{"title":"http://www.dot.state.wy.us/home/travel/scenic\\_byways.html","target":"http://www.dot.state.wy.us/home/travel/scenic_byways.html \"(opens in a new window","line":173},{"title":"http://www.dot.state.wy.us/files/live/sites/wydot/files/shared/Public%20Affairs/photos/Scenic%20Byways%20brochure%202013.pdf","target":"http://www.dot.state.wy.us/files/live/sites/wydot/files/shared/Public%20Affairs/photos/Scenic%20Byways%20brochure%202013.pdf \"(opens in a new window","line":174},{"title":"Park County Archives","target":"http://www.parkcounty.us/historicalarchives/historicalarchives.html \"(opens in a new window","line":178},{"title":"the Henry Ford museum","target":"https://www.thehenryford.org/collections-and-research/digital-collections/artifact/7445#slide=gs-213219 \"(opens in a new window","line":179},{"title":"national map of transcontinental routes","target":"https://www.loc.gov/resource/g3701p.ct001837/?r=0.108,0.052,0.429,0.212,0 \"(opens in a new window","line":180},{"title":"map of the Custer Battlefield Highway","target":"https://www.wdl.org/en/item/16782/view/1/1/ \"(opens in a new window","line":180},{"title":"map of the Park-to-Park highway","target":"http://www.americanroads.us/routemaps/Natl_Park-to-Park_Map_1922.jpg \"(opens in a new window","line":181},{"title":"American Heritage Center","target":"https://digitalcollections.uwyo.edu/luna